# Australia Electoral Rolls — every Zubrinich entry, read in full.
#
# 16 September 2026, on the month's subscription. FIFTY transcripts, NINETEEN
# people, three roll years (1939, 1941, 1943) in South Australia and two earlier
# ones (1913, 1935) in New South Wales. The trial of 13-14 September read eight
# of these and expired; searched.json has been carrying the rest as PENDING ever
# since. This is that row finished.
#
# WHY A ROLL IS WORTH MORE THAN AN INDEX ENTRY. The index gives a name, a year
# and a state. The transcript gives an OCCUPATION, a STREET ADDRESS and the
# OTHER PEOPLE AT THAT ADDRESS — which is a household claim, the same claim a
# house number makes in a Lika baptism and a plot number makes in a cemetery.
# Read three roll years together and you watch a household move.
#
# THE TRANSCRIPTION IS FINDMYPAST'S, NOT THIS ARCHIVE'S, AND IT SLIPS. Emma's
# 1941 occupation reads «Blamed» where 1939 and 1943 both read «Married».
# Eveline's 1935 address reads «178'M11rt0i1 Street». Una's 1939 address reads
# «Blanche, 11 Queen Street» — her own second given name has run into the
# address column. These are recorded EXACTLY AS THE SITE GIVES THEM, with the
# reading noted separately, because an OCR slip is evidence about the index and
# not about the family.
#
# given|year|occupation|address|sub-district|district|state|household at that address
